@author "Enrico Ehrich"
@$VER: llm_coding_cli.guide 1.0 (27.10.2026)
@smartwrap

@node main "Coding CLI as an LLM"
@{h1}Coding CLI as an LLM

A coding CLI -- Claude Code or Antigravity -- answers an agent's model call.
The agent runs as always: its prompt, its history, the hooks that add to it,
its session and its cancel. Only the call to the model goes elsewhere: to a
@{tt}coding_cli@{utt} instance, which runs the CLI on the operator's
subscription. The CLI reads the conversation as one task, runs its own tool
loop with the tools its workdir hands it through the MCP gateway, and its
final answer becomes the agent's assistant message.

@{code}
For developers
  @{"  Setting it up  " link setup}
  @{"  What one call does  " link call}
  @{"  What the model sees  " link model}
  @{"  When the next link answers  " link fallback}
  @{"  Known gaps  " link gaps}
@{body}
@endnode

@node setup "Setting it up"
@{h1}Setting it up

@{h2}The model entry

The provider is @{tt}claude_code@{utt} or @{tt}antigravity@{utt}; @{tt}model@{utt}
names the coding_cli instance. Nothing else of the entry is used -- model,
effort and the subscription threshold are the instance's, and a dialect key
set here is named in the log as ignored.

@{code yaml}
llm_system:
  models:
    cli_model:
      provider: claude_code
      model: my_claude_instance      # a coding_cli instance
  profiles:
    on_subscription:
      model_ref: cli_model
@{body}

Put the profile first in an agent's chain and an API profile after it: the
chain moves on when the CLI cannot answer.

@{h2}The instance

@{bullet}Its @{tt}cli@{utt} matches the provider (@{tt}claude@{utt} for
claude_code, @{tt}antigravity@{utt} for antigravity), or every call falls
back with an error in the log.
@{bullet}It has exactly one workdir: the call names none. A workdir with a
@{tt}gateway@{utt} gives the CLI that gateway's tools. The agent run's tool
bindings (@{tt}Agent.run_events(tool_bindings=...)@{utt}, a sub-agent's
spawn) go to the run as its @{tt}pin@{utt}, so the CLI's tool calls are held
to the same values as the agent's own; a run without bindings sends none. A
workdir whose gateway requires values (@{tt}pin@{utt}) refuses a run that
does not bring them, and the chain falls back.
@{bullet}The calling account is in its @{tt}allowed_users@{utt}.
@{bullet}@{tt}max_task_chars@{utt} holds the whole conversation: the task is the
system prompt and the history as text, and coding_cli refuses a longer one
(20 000 characters unless set) -- every call then falls back.
@{bullet}@{tt}max_result_chars@{utt} holds the longest final answer the agent
needs: a cut answer falls back.

The instance runs in the API process; an agent running elsewhere finds none
and falls back.
@endnode

@node call "What one call does"
@{h1}What one call does

@{bullet}It needs the agent run around it: its request id, user and session
(the session as @{tt}current_run_session@{utt}, set by every agent run). The
CLI's tool calls run in that session -- a store's documents are the agent's
own, as with its own calls. Without them the call falls back.
@{bullet}The first call of an agent run starts a run:
@{tt}<instance>_run_task@{utt} with the conversation as the task, @{tt}wake:
false@{utt}, the account, the session and the request id (the run's grant
and status are filed under it). While the run goes on,
@{tt}<instance>_get_run@{utt} waits for it, 600 seconds at a time, with
@{tt}stop_if_cancelled@{utt}.
@{bullet}A later call of the same session -- a nudge or a format correction
in the same agent run, the next turn of a continued sub-agent (a new agent run,
built anew) -- resumes the run it goes on from with only the messages added
since: when the conversation it gets is one it gave before, grown (the longest
such one). The CLI's own answer, as the agent kept it, is not sent again. A
history compacted in between, another conversation (a hook's own model call),
another user or session, or nothing new starts a run of its own; so does a run
coding_cli will not resume (its worktree busy, other bindings) -- with the whole
conversation, not a move down the chain. The runs a session may go on with are
kept in this process: after a restart its next call starts afresh.
@{bullet}Cancelling the agent cancels the wait, and coding_cli stops a run
whose waiting caller is cancelled.
@{bullet}The answer: the run's final text as the assistant message, no tool
calls, @{tt}served_by@{utt} @{tt}<provider>:<instance>@{utt}. Usage reports
cost 0 -- the subscription pays -- and the run's tokens: prompt tokens with
the cache's reads and writes among them, and the output, summed by the CLI
over its own model calls -- one run is one call, however many turns the CLI
took inside it. Claude Code's counts are read as Anthropic's API names them
(its @{tt}input_tokens@{utt} holds only what neither came from nor went into
the cache); agy counts its cache reads beside its input as well
(@{tt}cache_read_tokens@{utt}), its thinking inside its output. Being a sum, they are
not how full the agent's context is: the usage says
@{tt}reflects_context: false@{utt}, the usage store keeps the call as one
without a conversation (in its totals and cache share, never as the context
reading), and the chat's footer shows no fill for it. A run that ended
without a result (stopped, killed) reports none: its stream carries no
output count to sum. The message debugger sees the call through the
same notices as any client: the task as the payload, the run's answer as the
response, the CLI's model as the model.
@endnode

@node model "What the model sees"
@{h1}What the model sees

The CLI gets one task text, built from the messages in their order:

@{code}
# Instructions

<the system prompt>

## user

<a user message, hook insertions included>

## assistant

<an earlier answer>
[called <tool> with <arguments>]

## tool

<a tool result>
@{body}

The agent's tool list is not passed: the CLI has the tools of its workdir.
A part of a message that is not text (an image) is named, not passed:
@{tt}[image_url not passed on]@{utt}. A resumed run gets only the blocks of
the messages added since its last call.

@{h2}Token and cache effect

None on the agent's own requests: nothing is added to its prompt or history.
The CLI's own context is the CLI's.
@endnode

@node fallback "When the next link answers"
@{h1}When the next link answers

@{table}
Case | Raised | The chain
the subscription's limit (coding_cli's limit field) | LLMQuotaExhaustedError | blocks this link until the limit resets (when coding_cli knows it), then moves on
not started for another reason (runs still going, git, the gateway) | LLMServerError | moves on, no block
an agy run that failed on its login before its first turn | LLMServerError, if it fails again | starts once more after 15 s first; failed again, moves on, and for ten minutes no run of that user on that instance starts twice (a run that answers ends that)
an agy run that ended without an answer on a refused step (a command, say: agy then ends its whole conversation) | LLMServerError, if it ends so again | resumed once, told that such steps are refused and to go on with its other tools (measured for a command: it answers then); a second such end moves on. The call's usage holds both runs
a Claude Code run that did not reach its API (api_error connection_failed; measured: DNS gone, ENOTFOUND after about 3 min) | LLMConnectionError, caused by the error its code names | moves on; when no link of the step's chain reached a provider and one found no route, the step waits for the network (network_outage_seconds) -- a refused connection (ECONNREFUSED) is no outage
a run that failed, was stopped or was cancelled | LLMServerError | moves on, no block
an answer cut by max_result_chars, or none | LLMServerError | moves on, no block
the instance missing, or another cli than the provider's | LLMServerError | moves on, no block
no agent run around the call | LLMServerError | moves on, no block
@{body}

A failed run without tokens says nothing of the network (agy with the network gone fails at once on an
unknown model): it does not count as a provider that got the request, so a link before or after it decides
whether the step waits for the network. A run that counted tokens, an answer cut or empty, did reach its model.

Each of them logs one line naming the provider, the instance and why; a
mismatched cli logs it as an error. Antigravity reports no subscription
windows: a run it stops at its limit is expected to arrive as a failed run
(not measured yet), which moves the chain on without a block.
@endnode

@node gaps "Known gaps"
@{h1}Known gaps

@{bullet}A workdir whose gateway fixes values is not supported.
@{bullet}The tools are the workdir's, not the agent's: a tool the agent has
but the gateway does not hand on (a sub-agent manager) is missing for the
CLI. Say so in the prompt the agent renders for this profile.
@{bullet}One process: the instance must run where the agent runs.
@{bullet}One more resume after an agy run that ended on a refused step: a call
that needs it takes as long as two runs, and the second sees the note, not
the step's refusal itself.
@{bullet}Every CLI run is a coding_cli run with a worktree and a branch of its
own, which coding_cli does not remove. As an LLM link that is one per agent
run: give the instance a small repository of its own as its workdir, and
clear its worktrees now and then (coding_cli guide).
@{bullet}No streaming: the answer arrives when the run ends.
@endnode
